WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.888
Think of the heart as two pumps connected in series, not four unrelated rooms. The venae cavae return systemic venous blood to the right atrium. The right ventricle sends it through the pulmonary artery to the lungs. Pulmonary veins return oxygenated blood to the left atrium.
把心脏理解为串联的两个泵，而不是四个互不相关的房间。腔静脉将体静脉血送入右心房；右心室经肺动脉将血送至肺；肺静脉把氧合血送回左心房。

00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:35.976
The left ventricle then ejects through the aorta into the systemic circulation. Its thicker muscular wall reflects the greater pressure required for that task. Artery and vein describe direction of flow relative to the heart, not whether the blood contains more oxygen.
左心室再经主动脉向体循环射血，其较厚的心肌反映该任务所需的较高压力。动脉、静脉按相对于心脏的流向命名，不是按含氧量命名。

00:00:35.976 --> 00:00:58.224
Follow a drop of blood through the right heart: right atrium, tricuspid valve, right ventricle, pulmonic valve, pulmonary artery. On its return: pulmonary veins, left atrium, mitral valve, left ventricle, aortic valve, aorta. Say the sequence without swapping the two sides.
沿右心追踪一滴血：右心房、三尖瓣、右心室、肺动脉瓣、肺动脉。返回后依次为肺静脉、左心房、二尖瓣、左心室、主动脉瓣、主动脉。练习时不要把左右两侧互换。

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:17.568
Valves move because the pressure gradient changes. During ventricular contraction, AV valves close; papillary muscles and chordae restrain their leaflets from prolapsing backwards. They do not actively open the valves. Regurgitation means that the intended one-way barrier is leaking.
瓣膜因压力梯度变化而运动。心室收缩时房室瓣关闭，乳头肌和腱索限制瓣叶向后脱垂，并不是主动拉开瓣膜。反流表示原本单向的屏障发生漏流。

00:01:17.568 --> 00:01:35.400
From inside outward, identify endocardium, myocardium and epicardium. The epicardium is also the visceral layer of the pericardium. The pericardial sac surrounds the heart, with a small lubricated space that normally allows low-friction movement.
从内到外辨认心内膜、心肌和心外膜。心外膜也是心包的脏层。心包囊包围心脏，正常时少量润滑液所在的间隙使心脏低摩擦运动。

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:55.464
A problem outside the muscle can still compromise the pump. Pericardial inflammation causes irritation, while pressure from a significant effusion may impede filling. An ECG does not directly measure the volume of that fluid or prove that filling is adequate; bedside assessment remains essential.
心肌外的问题也能妨碍泵功能。心包炎可造成刺激；显著积液产生的压力可能阻碍充盈。心电图不直接测量积液量，也不能证明充盈充足，因此仍须结合床旁评估。

00:01:55.464 --> 00:02:14.280
Ventricular diastole allows relaxation and filling. Ventricular systole includes pressure generation and ejection. The shorthand that semilunar valves are open during systole describes ejection; there are also brief isovolumetric phases when all valves are closed.
心室舒张包括松弛和充盈；心室收缩包括建立压力和射血。“收缩期半月瓣开放”的简化说法指射血阶段；此外还有短暂的等容期，所有瓣膜均关闭。

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:35.736
The first heart sound, S1, accompanies closure of the mitral and tricuspid valves. S2 accompanies closure of the aortic and pulmonic valves. Electrical depolarization triggers subsequent mechanical activity, but a visible QRS does not guarantee an effective pulse or adequate cardiac output.
第一心音 S1 与二尖瓣、三尖瓣关闭有关；第二心音 S2 与主动脉瓣、肺动脉瓣关闭有关。电去极化触发随后的机械活动，但出现 QRS 不保证有有效脉搏或足够心输出量。

00:02:35.736 --> 00:02:54.960
Coronary arteries arise near the aortic root and supply the working heart muscle itself. The left main divides into the left anterior descending and circumflex arteries. Use anterior and septal territory for the LAD, and lateral territory for the circumflex, as an introductory map.
冠状动脉起自主动脉根部附近，供应心肌自身。左主干分为前降支和回旋支。入门时可把前降支联系前壁、室间隔，把回旋支联系侧壁。

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:13.416
The right coronary artery often supplies the inferior left ventricular wall and important nodal tissue. This helps explain why inferior ischemia and slowed conduction may coexist. Coronary dominance varies, so a single rhythm strip cannot establish which artery is obstructed.
右冠状动脉常供应左心室下壁及重要结区，因此下壁缺血可能与传导减慢并存。但冠脉优势型存在差异，不能凭单一节律条确定哪条血管阻塞。

00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:33.528
Gap junctions connect neighbouring cardiac cells so activation can spread. Specialized conduction structures organize that spread into a useful sequence. Without coordination, electrical activity may continue while effective pumping fails. This is the bridge from anatomy to rhythm interpretation.
缝隙连接使相邻心肌细胞之间能够传递激动，特殊传导结构又把传播组织成有用的顺序。缺乏协调时，电活动可能继续，而有效泵血却失败；这正是解剖知识与节律判读之间的联系。

00:03:33.528 --> 00:03:52.968
When you explain an ECG finding, complete the chain: where activation begins, how it spreads, what contraction should follow, and what the patient actually demonstrates. Pulse quality, mentation, skin and pressure supply evidence that the electrical drawing alone cannot provide.
解释心电图时，应说完整因果链：激动从哪里开始、如何传播、理应产生什么收缩，以及患者实际上表现如何。脉搏质量、意识、皮肤和血压提供电图本身没有的证据。
